Subject: [PATCH 9/9] The Wardrobe and the Shop work for an offline name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pages signed every offline name in with Microsoft: wardrobe_account
took only a selected Microsoft account, so both pages answered with the
sign-in plate instead of the wardrobe.

The offline name now has an account of its own there (the name and the
vanilla offline UUID the game plays with), its outfit kept on this disk
as any account's is. Its refresh asks the service for the catalogue and
the item files when it answers, keeps the last ones when it doesn't, and
owns everything the catalogue lists — nothing is asked of Mojang, whose
session an offline name cannot prove. Equipping shows at once, waits on
this disk alone, and the game is told what it wears and whether it owns
cosmetics all the same. The preview wears the skin the player picked for
the name (skins/<name>.png), 64×64.
